deliberately remain in their original location."], ["you keep the cup. your claw stops over the crack. “the problem can wait.” you tuck the broken piece into the crevice. “not this one.”", "you look at the broken cup. “the cup. the cup. the same cup. the same. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it. you can keep it"], ["you turn your head toward the noise, then take one step backward. you listen without touching the fence. the sound continues. you stay where you are.", "you turn your head. the noise is loud. you can hear the rain on the step, the creak of the fence, and the faint smell of rain in the air. you look at the corner. there is no place where the noise can be heard. you can hear it from here. you can hear it from the corner. you can hear it from the corner. you will leave it there."], ["you crouch at the threshold. “same.” you change one thing: the claw stays on the step instead of the wall. you wait for the voice. the door remains open.", "i crouch and bring my claw to the threshold. the door is open. the same open door. i wait for the voice to come from there. then i bring my claw close to the wall. the voice is not there. the door is still open. i bring it close to my face. the same face. the same face."], ["you look at the stranger. your claw points to the corner. “there.” you move your seed tin closer to your body. the stranger sits. you keep one eye on the door.", "you look at the stranger. “you are not here. you are here. you came here. you are not here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here. you are here"], ["you leave the cup in your palm. “no corner.” you turn it once. “the lid was wrong.” you look at the floorboards. “the floor has a lid.” you set the cup down and listen.", "you put the cup in the palm of your hand. “i put it in the corner. the corner. the corner. the corner. the corner. the corner.” you look at the cup. “the corner has a lid. the lid has a lid. the corner has a lid.” you put the cup back in the palm of your hand. “the corner has a lid. the corner has a lid. the corner has a lid.” you put the cup back in the corner. “the corner has a lid. the corner has a lid.” you put the cup back in the corner. “the corner has a lid. the corner has a lid.” you put the cup back in the corner. “the corner has a lid. the corner has a lid.” you put the cup"], ["you look at the bent nail. “worse.” you press the loose end into the board, then stop. you keep your claw off it. the nail stays where you made it worse.", "you look at the broken nail. “it was there. the same nail. the same. you saw it, and you saw it. you know where it is. you know where it was. you know where it was used. you know where it is now. you know where it was. you know where it was used. you know where it is now. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know where it was. you know"], ["you look at the broken half. “not that.” you put it down. “the first thing was...” you stop. your claw finds the first seed in your pocket. “this was first.”", "you look at the broken half. “the original goal. the original plan. the original plan. you know the plan. you know the order. you know the order. you know the order. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it. you know it."], ["you look at the broken wheel. the rim is loose again. you do not put it back. you turn the wheel once and listen. “same place. wrong place.” you set it beside the nail.", "i look at the broken wheel. the rim is gone, but the wheel is still there. i put it in the crevice, where it can wait. then i look at the broken nail. it was there. the same nail. i put it in the crevice, too. the nail stays. the wheel stays."], ["you hold the box on your knee. “summer.” you put that note on the step. “winter.” you put that note in the corner. the box gets smaller. the labels do not agree.", "you put the box in the corner. the labels are wrong. the first label says \"summer.\" the second says \"summer.\" the third says \"summer.\" you put the fourth label on the step. \"summer,\" you say, then stop. \"no.\" you put the fourth label on the step. \"summer.\" you put the third label on the step. \"summer.\" you put the fifth label on the step. \"summer.\" you put the sixth label on the step. \"summer.\" you put the seventh label on the step. \"summer.\" you put the eighth label on the step. \"summer.\" you put the tenth label on the step. \"winter.\" you put the eleventh label on the step. \"winter.\" you put the twelfth label on the step. \"winter"], ["you read the phrase once. you draw a line under it. “this means everything.” you tap the page